      "content": "Major international museums provide unparalleled resources for advanced scholarly research that smaller, national institutions often cannot match. These institutions house vast, curated collections that allow for comparative studies across diverse civilizations, creating a richer, more comprehensive narrative of human history. Furthermore, these world-class facilities maintain the highest standards of conservation science, ensuring the long-term preservation of fragile cultural heritage for future generations.",
      "source": "target",
